## Module 5 — Microsoft 365 Copilot Ecosystem

**Objectives:** enterprise vs. consumer Copilot · the 3 licensing tiers · map tasks to apps · Copilot Studio & Graph · Researcher vs. Analyst · Build/Buy/Extend

| | M365 Copilot (enterprise) | Consumer Copilot |
|---|---|---|
| Data reach | Org data via Microsoft Graph | Public info + user content only |
| Security | Existing controls, role-based access | No tenant governance |
| Choose when | Internal data & compliance needs | Only public info needed |

| | M365 Copilot Chat | M365 Copilot (add-on) |
|---|---|---|
| Cost | Included with M365 | Paid, per-user/month |
| Grounding | Web only + uploaded files | Web + work data via Graph |
| In-app Copilot | No | Yes (Word/Excel/PPT/Outlook/Teams) |
| Researcher & Analyst | No | Yes |

**Task → app mapping:**

| Task signal | App |
|---|---|
| "Draft a report" | Word |
| "Analyse sales data" | Excel |
| "Build a deck" | PowerPoint |
| "Summarise this thread" | Outlook |
| "Recap a meeting" | Teams |

**Copilot Studio:** low-code platform for custom topics/flows connected to internal data — "the middle ground" between out-of-box Copilot and full custom Azure AI development.

**Microsoft Graph:** connects M365 data so Copilot retrieves relevant context in real time — permission-trimmed, only returns data the user can already access.

| | Researcher | Analyst |
|---|---|---|
| Use for | Investigating, synthesising, comparing | Analysing metrics, interpreting numbers |
| Signal words | research, summarise, explore, compare | analyse, evaluate, trends, metrics |

**Build / Buy / Extend:** start with **Buy** → **Extend** only when needed → **Build** only as a last resort.

**The integrated Microsoft AI solution** — Copilot + Graph + Identity + Compliance + Responsible AI combined into ONE system. This is why Microsoft 365 Copilot is preferred over standalone third-party AI tools whenever security, governance, or organisational data are involved: it inherits identity-based access, permission-trimming, DLP, auditing, and content safety automatically — built in, not bolted on.

**Copilot licensing by adoption stage:**

| Copilot licensing | Best for |
|---|---|
| Included with M365 | Early exploration, low barrier |
| Monthly per-user (add-on) | Daily use, core productivity roles |
| Pay-as-you-go (linked to Azure subscription) | Pilots, variable usage |

> ⚠️ **Don't confuse Copilot licensing with Azure AI/Foundry subscription models** (see Module 8) — they're two separate systems. A prepaid/committed-capacity model belongs to Azure AI workloads, not Copilot end-user licensing.

**Agent types (when a scenario asks you to build one):**

| Agent type | When to use |
|---|---|
| Declarative agent | Low-code/no-code, built in Copilot Studio, follows predefined instructions, grounded in M365 data via Graph — no developer required |
| Custom engine agent | Needs a developer — custom orchestration/model, capabilities beyond declarative |
| Microsoft Copilot Chat | Not a buildable agent type — it's the built-in general chat experience itself |

**✅ Knowledge check**
- Q: Scenario mentions internal data, security, compliance. **A: Microsoft 365 Copilot**
- Q: "Evaluate the trends and metrics." Use: **A: Analyst**
- Q: Copilot must follow business logic, connect to internal systems. **A: Extend (via Copilot Studio)**
- Q: Why choose an integrated Microsoft AI solution over a standalone AI tool? **A: It inherits identity access, permission-trimming, DLP, auditing & content safety automatically**
- Q: No developer budget, predefined instructions, M365-grounded — what agent type? **A: Declarative agent**

