## Module 6 — Foundry Tools & Matching a Model

**Objectives:** know when to reach for Foundry Tools · name the key services · match generative vs. ML models to a need

**Copilot is for USING AI. Foundry is for RUNNING and MANAGING AI at scale.** Reach for Foundry Tools when a scenario needs custom models, RAG pipelines, multi-step orchestration, or lifecycle governance.

| Service | What it does |
|---|---|
| Azure AI services | Prebuilt APIs — vision, speech, language — no training required |
| Azure Vision | Image/video analysis, OCR, visual inspection |
| Azure AI Search | Intelligent discovery — powers RAG patterns |
| Azure Document Intelligence | Extracts structured data from documents (forms, invoices, contracts) |
| Azure Content Understanding | Extracts structured fields from documents/content and organizes output for reporting/analytics — related to, but distinct from, Document Intelligence |
| Microsoft Foundry | Unified platform to build/deploy/manage AI under governance |

> ⚠️ **Watch the extraction-tool traps:** model fine-tuning and prompt flow are NEVER the answer to an "extract fields / structure data" question — fine-tuning adjusts model behaviour, prompt flow orchestrates workflows. Neither extracts or structures data.

| Generative models | Traditional ML models |
|---|---|
| LLMs — drafting, summarising, reasoning | Regression/classification/clustering |
| Best for natural language, code, creative content | Best for precise predictions, scoring, patterns |

Also recognise: **SLMs** (small, cheap, fast, on-device) and **embedding models** (power semantic search/RAG retrieval).

**Foundry at enterprise scale:** a unified platform for building, deploying, and managing AI — supports scaling from pilot to production without redesign. Security/governance are core differentiators: identity-based access, encryption, monitoring, policy enforcement. Choose Foundry when AI must be managed reliably over time, not just implemented once.

**✅ Knowledge check**
- Q: Custom models, RAG pipelines, lifecycle governance needed. **A: Foundry Tools**
- Q: Extract structured fields from thousands of contracts and prepare for reporting. **A: Azure Content Understanding (or Document Intelligence, depending on options given) — never fine-tuning or prompt flow**

