## Module 7 — Responsible AI & Governance

**Objectives:** recall all 6 Responsible AI standards · distinguish Fairness from Inclusiveness · explain AI governance & the AI council

**Why responsible AI matters:** it's foundational, not optional — the core purpose is building trust while preventing harm and risk. **Human accountability:** AI assists, but humans always remain responsible for the decisions it informs — this is tested directly on the exam.

| Standard | What it requires |
|---|---|
| Fairness | Must not systematically disadvantage individuals/groups |
| Inclusiveness | Everyone can use and benefit from the system |
| Reliability & Safety | Accurate, dependable, fails safely |
| Privacy & Security | Personal/sensitive data protected throughout |
| Transparency | Users know AI is involved and how it influences outcomes |
| Accountability | Decisions are explainable, reviewable, clearly owned |

> ⚠️ **The classic trap:** Fairness = outcomes don't harm a group. Inclusiveness = everyone CAN use and benefit. These are constantly confused on the exam.

**AI governance** defines rules for how AI is developed, deployed, monitored, and retired — the full lifecycle.

**The AI council** is a cross-functional group (business, IT, legal, security, compliance) setting strategy, reviewing compliance/ethics, monitoring risk — preventing fragmented, ad-hoc adoption.

**Preventive vs. detective controls:** when a scenario asks for a safeguard to intervene on high-risk AI actions, favor built-in, real-time controls (RBAC tied to identity, kill-switches) over "periodic manual review" — periodic review is detective (catches problems after the fact), not preventative.

**✅ Knowledge check**
- Q: AI gives worse recommendations to one demographic group. **A: Fairness**
- Q: A group technically has access but can't effectively use the tool. **A: Inclusiveness**
- Q: Company requires identity-based access, traceability, and a safeguard to intervene on high-risk events. **A: RBAC integrated with organisational identity + controlled real-time intervention — not periodic manual review**

